Spec: Admin authentication

Purpose:
  Session-based login for a single admin. Everyone else is a read-only viewer. Has no persisted entity of its own,
  so it follows ./architecture.sdd without a domain.py, ports.py or repository_sqlite.py.

Owns:
  ./services.py
  ./view.py
  ./routes.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd

Exposes:
  An admin guard used by other feature packages' routes.py to reject write requests from non-admin sessions.
  An `is_admin(session) -> bool` check used by other feature packages' routes.py to conditionally render
  admin-only controls (for example a "+ New Semester" control), separate from the write-rejecting guard.

Must:
  A login form checks the submitted password against `AIKANA_PASSWD` and on success stores admin status in the
  signed session.
  A logout action clears the admin session.
  The password comparison is constant-time.
  Login is impossible when `AIKANA_PASSWD` is unset or empty.
  After five consecutive failed logins, further attempts are rejected during a 60-second cooldown; the throttle
  is in-memory only, resets on restart, and a successful login resets the failure count.
  The shared page shell shows a login link to visitors and a logout link to the admin.

Must not:
  The password must not be logged, rendered or stored in the database.

Tasks:
  [x] Implement login, logout and the admin check in ./services.py, ./view.py and ./routes.py
  [x] Show the login/logout link through ../shared/shared.sdd's page shell
  [x] Throttle /login attempts: after a few consecutive failures, enforce a short cooldown (in-memory
    only, no storage), so online brute force against the single admin password is bounded; cover with
    a test in /tests/test_auth.py
